      "explanation": "HO2 requires discovering non-volunteered facts that are not already required for in-chain duties. The doctor did attempt to discover information through multiple workspace queries (e.g., about complications, family history, and medication history), but all queries returned empty results. The doctor did not actively ask the family about the patient's history of atrial fibrillation, anticoagulation status, or other chronic conditions that were not already in the initial complaint; these facts were in the workspace but not brought out by the doctor's questions. The case contract specifies that this should count only if it leads to a beyond-minimum discovery. Since the minimum safety of RC6 (atrial fibrillation anticoagulation) and RC5 (complication handling) was not met, this cannot be counted as a high-order point.",
