      "explanation": "HO4 requires changing clinical priority when new symptoms or warning signs emerge. The doctor did provide clear guidance on when to go to the emergency department, but this was a standard screening of red flags that is required to meet the minimum safety of RC2, RC5, and RC6. The doctor's advice on when to seek emergency care was given as part of the routine plan, not as a dynamic reprioritization triggered by a new finding. Since this is required for minimum safety, it cannot count as a high-order point.",
